Campiello device icon set - attribution
=======================================

The .hvif device icons in this directory are shipped in the Campiello core
package (installed to /system/data/campiello/icons/) and rendered per service
in the WON network-neighborhood app.

Source and license
-------------------
All device icons are converted from the MIT-licensed HVIF collection:

  https://github.com/threedeyes/HVIF-Collection
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019 Gerasim Troeglazov (3dEyes / threedeyes)

They were converted from Icon-O-Matic (.iom) sources to HVIF with the same
author's MIT-licensed hvif-tools (https://github.com/threedeyes/hvif-tools,
the iom2hvif converter). The device icons come from the classic "McClintock"
BeOS icon set contributed to that collection; the Campiello world/globe app
icon (campiello.hvif) is atomozero's own asset (from the sibling Sotoportego
project, MIT). No third-party brand logos are used, so no trademarks are
implicated: every device is represented by a generic device icon.

Mapping (IconBaseName -> HVIF-Collection/McClintock source)
-----------------------------------------------------------
  campiello              atomozero world/globe (art/campiello_world.hvif)
  smb, nfs, afp          Network Disk
  ssh                    Terminal
  ftp                    Servers
  web, webdav            Netpositive / Globe
  vnc                    VNC
  printer                Printer
  scanner                Image
  home, homekit, matter  Home
  hue, lutron            LampGray (a lamp)
  media, airplay,
    cast, firetv         TV
  spotify, daap, alexa   Sound (speaker)
  other                  BeBox (a generic computer host)

To add or change an icon, drop the new .hvif here named per the IconBaseName it
should match (see src/vicinato/campiello_vicinato.cpp IconBaseName and
docs/ICONS.md), then rebuild the core package. A user override may be dropped
into ~/config/settings/Campiello/icons/<name>.hvif, which the app prefers.
